---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TopBar from "@/components/TopBar.astro";
import { PRESETS } from "@/lib/sar/presets";
import { PATTERNS } from "@/lib/sar/compare";

// Interactive companion to the Math IA: a constant-airspeed Archimedean
// search spiral for a maritime SAR drone, with wind, current and a battery
// constraint. All of the simulation lives in src/lib/sar/ (DOM-free, so it can
// be reused for a scroll-animation easter egg); the UI lives in
// src/scripts/sar/.

const sliders = {
  drone: [
    { key: "U", label: "Airspeed", sym: "U", min: 6, max: 30, step: 0.5, unit: "m/s", tip: "Speed relative to the air. The model holds |v_air| = U constant all mission." },
    { key: "enduranceMin", label: "Endurance", sym: "T", min: 5, max: 60, step: 1, unit: "min", tip: "Total flight time the pack supports at airspeed U." },
    { key: "reservePct", label: "Landing reserve", sym: "", min: 0, max: 40, step: 1, unit: "%", tip: "Battery left on touchdown. Bingo is called so the drone lands with exactly this." },
    { key: "delay", label: "Takeoff delay", sym: "t_delay", min: 0, max: 180, step: 5, unit: "s", tip: "Alert → wheels-up. The datum keeps drifting meanwhile." },
    { key: "Rs", label: "Scan radius", sym: "Rs", min: 10, max: 120, step: 1, unit: "m", tip: "Half the camera's swath. Sets the spiral pitch b = Rs/π so arms sit exactly 2Rs apart." },
    { key: "r0k", label: "Start radius", sym: "r0", min: -0.5, max: 1, step: 0.05, unit: "×Rs", tip: "r0 = 0 starts on the datum; r0 = −0.5Rs double-covers the centre (see §3.2)." },
  ],
  scene: [
    { key: "datumDist", label: "Datum range", sym: "", min: 0.2, max: 6, step: 0.05, unit: "km", tip: "Distance from home to the last known position. You can also drag the markers on the map." },
    { key: "datumBrg", label: "Datum bearing", sym: "", min: 0, max: 359, step: 1, unit: "°", tip: "Bearing from home to the last known position." },
    { key: "sigma", label: "Probability spread", sym: "σ", min: 50, max: 1500, step: 10, unit: "m", tip: "Spread of the Gaussian likelihood around the datum, used to score probability of detection (POD)." },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout title="SAR search spiral · Luc Desautels" description="Interactive model of a constant-airspeed Archimedean search spiral for a maritime search-and-rescue drone — wind, current, battery and all.">
  <TopBar tone="dark" />

  <main class="sar" id="main" data-rsec="sar">
    <header class="sar__head">
      <div class="sar__head-l">
        <div class="sar__eyebrow">// RESEARCH · MATH AA IA · INTERACTIVE MODEL</div>
        <h1 class="sar__title">The search <em>spiral</em><span class="sar__dot">.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <p class="sar__lede">
        A maritime rescue drone has to search the most likely water first, while the water itself drifts, the wind pushes it
        sideways, and the battery counts down. This is the model from my Math IA — an Archimedean spiral re-parametrised so the
        drone holds a constant airspeed — running live. <span class="sar__lede-hint">Drag sliders, pick a scenario, scrub the timeline.</span>
      </p>
      <a class="sar__jump" href="#sar-notes">The math ↓</a>
    </header>

    <section class="sar__app" data-sar-app>
      <!-- ── Left: controls ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <aside class="sar__left" data-lenis-prevent aria-label="Simulation controls">
        <details class="sg" open>
          <summary class="sg__h"><span>Drone</span><i></i></summary>
          {sliders.drone.map((s) => (
            <label class="sl" data-tip={s.tip}>
              <span class="sl__top">
                <span class="sl__name">{s.label}{s.sym && <em class="sl__sym">{s.sym}</em>}</span>
                <output class="sl__val" data-out={s.key}></output>
              </span>
              <input type="range" min={s.min} max={s.max} step={s.step} data-k={s.key} data-unit={s.unit} />
            </label>
          ))}
          <div class="sg__note" data-bnote></div>
        </details>

        <details class="sg" open>
          <summary class="sg__h"><span>Wind &amp; current</span><i></i></summary>
          <div class="pads">
            <div class="pad" data-pad="wind" data-tip="Drag to set the wind. The arrow shows where the air is going; the readout is meteorological (the bearing it blows FROM).">
              <div class="pad__name">Wind <em class="sl__sym">v_wind</em></div>
              <canvas class="pad__c" width="130" height="130"></canvas>
              <output class="pad__val" data-padout="wind"></output>
            </div>
            <div class="pad" data-pad="cur" data-tip="Drag to set the surface current. It carries the survivor — and the datum — with it (bearing it sets TOWARD).">
              <div class="pad__name">Current <em class="sl__sym">v_c</em></div>
              <canvas class="pad__c" width="130" height="130"></canvas>
              <output class="pad__val" data-padout="cur"></output>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feas" data-feas data-tip="The spiral exists only while the drone out-runs the water relative to the air: |v_c − v_wind| < U.">
            <div class="feas__row"><span>|v_eff| = |v_c − v_wind|</span><b data-feas-val></b></div>
            <div class="feas__bar"><i data-feas-bar></i><span class="feas__lim"></span></div>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="sg" open>
          <summary class="sg__h"><span>Scene</span><i></i></summary>
          {sliders.scene.map((s) => (
            <label class="sl" data-tip={s.tip}>
              <span class="sl__top">
                <span class="sl__name">{s.label}{s.sym && <em class="sl__sym">{s.sym}</em>}</span>
                <output class="sl__val" data-out={s.key}></output>
              </span>
              <input type="range" min={s.min} max={s.max} step={s.step} data-k={s.key} data-unit={s.unit} />
            </label>
          ))}
          <label class="tg" data-tip="Head home the moment every target has been found instead of searching until bingo.">
            <input type="checkbox" data-k="stopOnContact" />
            <span class="tg__sw"></span><span>RTH when all targets found</span>
          </label>
        </details>

        <details class="sg">
          <summary class="sg__h"><span>Layers</span><i></i></summary>
          <div class="layers" data-layers>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="planned" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Planned spiral (water frame)</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="coverage" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Searched water</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="overlap" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Overlap shading</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="prob" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Probability field</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="swath" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Camera footprint</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="flow" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Wind &amp; current flow</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="future" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Future track</span></label>
            <label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" data-layer="reveal" checked /><span class="tg__sw"></span><span>Reveal targets before contact</span></label>
          </div>
        </details>

        <div class="sar__keys">
          <div><kbd>Space</kbd> play · <kbd>←</kbd><kbd>→</kbd> ±10 s · <kbd>[</kbd><kbd>]</kbd> events</div>
          <div><kbd>1</kbd><kbd>2</kbd><kbd>3</kbd> camera · <kbd>H</kbd> HUD · <kbd>C</kbd> compare</div>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- ── Centre: the map ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="sar__center">
        <div class="stage" data-stage data-lenis-prevent-wheel>
          <canvas class="stage__map" data-map></canvas>

          <div class="hud" data-hud>
            <!-- view controls -->
            <div class="cam" role="group" aria-label="Camera">
              <button type="button" data-cam="overview" class="is-on" title="Fit everything (1)">Overview</button>
              <button type="button" data-cam="drone" title="Follow the drone (2)">Drone</button>
              <button type="button" data-cam="datum" title="Lock to the drifting datum — the water's frame (3)">Datum</button>
              <span class="cam__sep"></span>
              <button type="button" data-drop title="Click the water to drop a target">⊕<span class="cam__lbl"> Target</span></button>
            </div>

            <!-- mode + clocks -->
            <div class="hp hp--mode" data-hp="mode">
              <div class="md">
                <span class="md__pill" data-md-pill>STANDBY</span>
                <span class="md__name" data-md-name>On the pad</span>
              </div>
              <div class="md__sub" data-md-sub></div>
              <div class="clk">
                <div class="clk__main"><span class="clk__k">T+</span><span data-clk>00:00</span></div>
                <div class="clk__ev" data-clk-prev></div>
                <div class="clk__ev clk__ev--next" data-clk-next></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- attitude -->
            <div class="hp hp--att" data-hp="att">
              <div class="att__hdg"><span>HDG</span><b data-att-hdg>000</b></div>
              <canvas class="att__ball" data-navball width="170" height="170"></canvas>
              <div class="att__row">
                <span>BANK <b data-att-bank>0°</b></span>
                <span>PITCH <b data-att-pitch>0°</b></span>
                <span>CRAB <b data-att-crab>0°</b></span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- battery -->
            <div class="hp hp--bat" data-hp="bat">
              <button class="hp__h" type="button" data-collapse title="Hover to peek, click to pin">Battery<i></i></button>
              <div class="hp__b">
                <div class="bat">
                  <div class="bat__pct"><b data-bat-pct>100</b><span>%</span></div>
                  <div class="bat__vis">
                    <div class="bat__bar" data-bat-bar>
                      <i class="bat__seg bat__seg--reserve" data-seg="reserve"></i>
                      <i class="bat__seg bat__seg--rth" data-seg="rth"></i>
                      <i class="bat__seg bat__seg--search" data-seg="search"></i>
                      <span class="bat__mk" data-bat-land title="Predicted landing charge"></span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bat__legend"><span class="k k--r">reserve</span><span class="k k--h">RTH need</span><span class="k k--s">search budget</span></div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="bat__sum" data-bat-sum></div>
                <dl class="kv kv--bat">
                  <dt>Flight left</dt><dd data-bat-left>—</dd>
                  <dt>RTH needs</dt><dd data-bat-rth>—</dd>
                  <dt>Search left</dt><dd data-bat-search>—</dd>
                  <dt>Lands with</dt><dd data-bat-land-txt>—</dd>
                  <dt>Still to cover</dt><dd data-bat-cover>—</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- telemetry -->
            <div class="hp hp--tel" data-hp="tel">
              <button class="hp__h" type="button" data-collapse title="Hover to peek, click to pin">Telemetry<i></i></button>
              <div class="hp__b">
                <div class="tel">
                  <dl class="kv">
                    <dt>AS</dt><dd data-tel="as">—</dd>
                    <dt>GS</dt><dd data-tel="gs">—</dd>
                    <dt>TRK</dt><dd data-tel="trk">—</dd>
                    <dt>POD</dt><dd data-tel="pod">—</dd>
                    <dt class="x">ALT</dt><dd class="x" data-tel="alt">—</dd>
                    <dt class="x" title="Headwind (H) or tailwind (T), and crosswind (X, + from the right)">WIND H/X</dt><dd class="x" data-tel="hw">—</dd>
                    <dt class="x">HOME</dt><dd class="x" data-tel="home">—</dd>
                    <dt class="x">DATUM</dt><dd class="x" data-tel="datum">—</dd>
                    <dt class="x">SEARCHED</dt><dd class="x" data-tel="area">—</dd>
                  </dl>
                  <canvas class="tel__env" data-env width="92" height="92" title="Wind (white) and current (teal) relative to the nose"></canvas>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- compare chip -->
            <button class="cmpchip" type="button" data-cmp-open title="Compare against other search patterns (C)">
              <span class="cmpchip__h">Compare patterns <i>↗</i></span>
              <span class="cmpchip__sum" data-cmp-sum></span>
              <span class="cmpchip__bars" data-cmp-bars></span>
            </button>

            <div class="toast" data-toast aria-live="polite"></div>
            <div class="warn" data-warn hidden></div>
            <div class="hint" data-hint>Drag <b>⌂ home</b> or <b>◇ LKP</b> to move them · scroll to zoom · drag to pan · double-click to reset</div>
          </div>

          <!-- compare drawer -->
          <div class="cmp" data-cmp hidden>
            <div class="cmp__head">
              <div>
                <div class="sar__eyebrow">// SAME DRONE · SAME INTERCEPT · SAME BATTERY</div>
                <h2 class="cmp__title">How the IA spiral stacks up</h2>
              </div>
              <button class="cmp__x" type="button" data-cmp-close aria-label="Close comparison">×</button>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp__legend" data-cmp-legend>
              {PATTERNS.map((p) => (
                <button type="button" class="lg is-on" data-series={p.id} title={p.blurb}>
                  <svg width="26" height="8" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="4" x2="25" y2="4" stroke={p.color} stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray={p.dash.join(" ")} /></svg>
                  <span>{p.short}</span>
                  <span class="lg__ghost" data-ghost={p.id} title="Show this pattern's ghost on the map">◌ map</span>
                </button>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="cmp__grid">
              <figure class="chart">
                <figcaption><b>Probability of detection</b> over the search <span>— the higher and earlier, the better</span></figcaption>
                <canvas data-chart="pod"></canvas>
              </figure>
              <figure class="chart">
                <figcaption><b>Distance from the datum</b> while searching <span>— likeliest water first means a steady climb (IA Fig. 5)</span></figcaption>
                <canvas data-chart="dist"></canvas>
              </figure>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp__multi" data-cmp-multi>
              {PATTERNS.map((p) => (
                <figure class="mini" data-mini={p.id}>
                  <canvas></canvas>
                  <figcaption><i style={`background:${p.color}`}></i>{p.short}<b data-mini-score></b></figcaption>
                </figure>
              ))}
            </div>
            <table class="cmp__table" data-cmp-table>
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Pattern</th><th title="AUC of POD vs an ideal disc growing at 2·Rs·U, perfectly in order">Search score</th><th title="How close the pattern's order is to likeliest-first, for the area it actually covered">Order</th><th>POD at bingo</th><th>50% POD</th><th>Targets</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody></tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="cmp__foot">
              Every pattern starts at the IA spiral's intercept and leaves at its own bingo (elapsed + RTH ≥ usable endurance). POD is scored in the
              water's frame against a Gaussian of spread σ around the drifting datum. The three spirals are the same equation solved in three frames:
              the water's (IA), the ground's (GPS-locked, ignores current) and the air's (ignores both).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- timeline -->
        <div class="tl" data-tl>
          <div class="tl__ctrl">
            <button type="button" data-tl-prev title="Previous event ([)" aria-label="Previous event">⏮</button>
            <button type="button" class="tl__play" data-tl-play title="Play / pause (Space)" aria-label="Play">▶</button>
            <button type="button" data-tl-next title="Next event (])" aria-label="Next event">⏭</button>
            <div class="tl__speed" role="group" aria-label="Playback speed" data-tl-speed>
              <button type="button" data-spd="1">1×</button>
              <button type="button" data-spd="5">5×</button>
              <button type="button" data-spd="15" class="is-on">15×</button>
              <button type="button" data-spd="40">40×</button>
              <button type="button" data-spd="100">100×</button>
            </div>
            <div class="tl__time"><b data-tl-now>00:00</b><span> / </span><span data-tl-end>00:00</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl__track" data-tl-track>
            <div class="tl__phases" data-tl-phases></div>
            <div class="tl__done" data-tl-done></div>
            <div class="tl__marks" data-tl-marks></div>
            <div class="tl__head" data-tl-head></div>
            <div class="tl__hover" data-tl-hover></div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl__legend">
            <span><i class="ph ph--0"></i>Standby</span>
            <span><i class="ph ph--1"></i>Intercept</span>
            <span><i class="ph ph--2"></i>Spiral search</span>
            <span><i class="ph ph--3"></i>Return to home</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── Right: scenarios + contacts ───────────────────────────── -->
      <aside class="sar__right" data-lenis-prevent aria-label="Scenarios">
        <div class="rh">Scenarios</div>
        <div class="presets" data-presets>
          {PRESETS.map((p) => (
            <button type="button" class="ps" data-preset={p.id}>
              <canvas class="ps__thumb" width="88" height="88" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
              <span class="ps__txt">
                <span class="ps__tag">{p.tag}</span>
                <span class="ps__name">{p.name}</span>
                <span class="ps__blurb">{p.blurb}</span>
              </span>
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="rh rh--c">Contacts <span data-contacts-count></span></div>
        <ul class="contacts" data-contacts></ul>
        <button type="button" class="ghostbtn" data-clear-targets>Clear targets</button>
      </aside>

      <div class="tip" data-tipbox role="tooltip"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Notes: the math ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="notes" id="sar-notes">
      <div class="notes__in">
        <div class="sar__eyebrow">// THE MODEL, IN FIVE LINES</div>
        <h2 class="notes__title">From a spiral to a flight plan</h2>
        <div class="notes__grid">
          <article class="eq">
            <span class="eq__n">01</span>
            <h3>An Archimedean spiral, pitched by the camera</h3>
            <p>Arms 2Rs apart leave no gaps and no overlap, so the pitch is fixed by the scan radius.</p>
            <math display="block"><mi>r</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mi>θ</mi></math>
          </article>
          <article class="eq">
            <span class="eq__n">02</span>
            <h3>Centred on a drifting datum</h3>
            <p>The survivor moves with the water, so the spiral does too.</p>
            <math display="block"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></math>
          </article>
          <article class="eq">
            <span class="eq__n">03</span>
            <h3>Hold the airspeed constant</h3>
            <p>The drone's speed through the air is fixed, whatever the wind and current are doing.</p>
            <math display="block"><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>w</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width="0.6em"/><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>wind</mi></msub></math>
          </article>
          <article class="eq eq--half">
            <span class="eq__n">04</span>
            <h3>…which is a quadratic in θ′</h3>
            <p>Take the + root. Because |v<sub>eff</sub>| &lt; U makes AC &lt; 0, √Δ &gt; |B|: it is always the positive one.</p>
            <math display="block"><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>
            <math display="block" class="eq__sub"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mspace width="0.3em"/><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width="0.3em"/><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>
          </article>
          <article class="eq eq--half">
            <span class="eq__n">05</span>
            <h3>Straight legs: intercept &amp; return</h3>
            <p>Out to the moving spiral start S(t) and back home, each at airspeed U. Smallest positive τ of:</p>
            <math display="block"><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><mi>τ</mi><mspace width="0.4em"/><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width="0.4em"/><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>
          </article>
          <article class="eq eq--wide">
            <span class="eq__n">06</span>
            <h3>The battery decides when the spiral ends</h3>
            <p>
              Rather than solving T = (t₁ − t<sub>delay</sub>) + (t₂ − t₁) + (t₃ − t₂) for θ(t₂) after the fact, the simulation checks it live: the drone
              leaves the spiral the instant <i>elapsed flight time + RTH time from here</i> reaches the usable endurance. That's exactly an autopilot's
              battery “bingo” — and it lands with the reserve you set, to the second.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <details class="refine">
          <summary>Refinements since the submitted paper</summary>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Straight legs.</b> The paper wrote the intercept and return times as a vector divided by a vector, (C₀ + v<sub>c</sub>t₁ − H)/(v<sub>air</sub> + v<sub>wind</sub>). Here each leg is the interception quadratic above (closed form), which also gives the heading to hold.</li>
            <li><b>Aim point.</b> The intercept targets the spiral's first point C(t₁) + (r₀, 0), not the datum itself — it only matters when r₀ ≠ 0.</li>
            <li><b>Root choice.</b> Choosing the + root isn't just “realistic”: whenever |v<sub>eff</sub>| &lt; U it is provably the only positive root. When |v<sub>eff</sub>| ≥ U no constant-airspeed spiral exists — the model now says so.</li>
            <li><b>Autonomous ODE.</b> θ′ depends on θ alone, so t(θ) is a plain integral ∫dθ/θ′(θ). No special ODE solver is needed; RK4 is used here only for even time-sampling.</li>
            <li><b>Appendix code.</b> The Streamlit prototype integrated θ′ = U/√(r² + b²) (the still-air formula) with the current bolted on afterwards, so its airspeed wasn't actually constant; its spiral was also centred v<sub>c</sub>·t₁ behind the datum. This page integrates the full quadratic.</li>
            <li><b>w(θ).</b> In §4.2 the line w(θ) = r′(θ)² + r(θ)·θ′ is a typo for the vector w(θ) = [r′cosθ − r sinθ, r′sinθ + r cosθ], with ‖w‖² = r² + r′². A(θ) was already right.</li>
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

